 "caveats": [
  "About ten trading sessions: the comparison shows how the mechanics behave, it cannot show that any strategy earns anything. A difference between strategies is not evidence.",
  "Every verdict is computed from a shuffled-score placebo: 'within the placebo range' means the result is what chance gives for this window.",
  "Annualised volatility is the ten-day standard deviation scaled by sqrt(252); it is a rough indication only. Costs are an illustrative one-way rate; no spreads, impact or taxes.",
  "The risk-limit strategy and the impact strategy are experiments with their parameters fixed in configs/rebalancer.yaml before any result existed; the impact model is itself experimental and a report's impact has no direction. They are never promoted to the baseline on the strength of this window.",
  "The sensitivity grid tries 21 settings. About two of them would fall outside their own 5th-95th placebo range by chance alone, so the best cell is the luckiest cell, not a recommendation: choosing it would be choosing after seeing the result. The shipped parameters were fixed before any result existed and are not changed by this grid.",
  "The benchmark is equal weight: the repo holds no market-cap data."
 ]
